(FIL-07: permissions returns the file's permission bits as a Number.
 LANGUAGE.md:3812's table entry is "File permission bits (e.g., 0644)" -
 an EXAMPLE, not a promised value, and the mode a fresh file lands at is
 umask-dependent: 420 (octal 0644) under umask 022, 384 (octal 0600)
 under a stricter 077. Asserting the literal 420 would file a false
 wrong-value finding on any machine or container with a different
 umask. What the manual DOES promise is the shape - a Number, and mode
 bits fit in three octal digits - so the assertion is a range, 0..511
 (0..0777), via 'gen file assert range quietly' (reused from FIL-05/
 FIL-06's leaf below rather than copied: same two-sided-bound, print-a-
 marker-not-the-value shape, here because the value is
 environment-dependent rather than wall-clock-dependent). Probe:
 docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-07.vox, which records 420 as the value
 OBSERVED under this machine's umask 022, not as the claim.)

