(FIL-46: Read line REPLACES the buffer with the next line, rather than
 appending to it - LANGUAGE.md:3977. A fixed-length seed is appended to
 the sink buffer first; if Read line appended instead of replacing, the
 final size would be seed length + line length + 1 (the newline), not
 line length + 1 - so the one post-read size check puts both the
 replace claim and the newline-retention claim (LANGUAGE.md:3995, not
 this batch's row, caught for free) on trial together, the same
 reasoning D2's probe used for plain `Read`. Probe:
 docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-53.vox.)

