(FIL-100: closing an already-closed file handle neither crashes nor sets
 the error flag (LANGUAGE.md:4194) - the double-free-is-impossible claim
 from the file-handle side. Incidentally the same *no-crash* observation
 FIL-86 needs for its own "no use-after-free" claim (LANGUAGE.md:4142),
 though this leaf is scoped to FIL-100 alone; FIL-86's tracking-mechanism
 half stays out of a generator's reach regardless. Probe: docs/ledger/
 probes/files/FIL-100.vox.)

